description:
Get what an asset depends on (dependencies) or what references it (referencers). Check before making breaking changes.

Examples:
- What references BP_Weapon: {"asset_path": "/Game/BP_Weapon", "direction": "referencers"}
- What does BP_Player use: {"asset_path": "/Game/BP_Player", "direction": "dependencies"}
- Full dependency tree: {"asset_path": "/Game/BP_Player", "direction": "dependencies", "recursive": true}
- Both directions: {"asset_path": "/Game/BP_Player", "direction": "both"}

Lifecycle operations on existing assets.

Actions:
- "duplicate": Copy asset. Requires new_name. Optional new_path (defaults to same folder).
- "rename": Rename asset in place. Requires new_name. Leaves a redirector.
- "move": Move asset to new folder. Requires new_path. Optional new_name.
- "delete": Delete asset. Checks for referencers first — refuses if any exist.
- "save": Save asset to disk.

Examples:
- {"action": "duplicate", "asset_path": "/Game/BP_Enemy", "new_name": "BP_EnemyRanged"}
- {"action": "rename", "asset_path": "/Game/BP_Old", "new_name": "BP_New"}
- {"action": "move", "asset_path": "/Game/BP_Temp", "new_path": "/Game/Characters"}
- {"action": "delete", "asset_path": "/Game/BP_Unused"}
- {"action": "save", "asset_path": "/Game/BP_Modified"}
